## Final Judgement
The key insight from the fact-check is that Dr. Anthony Fauci co-authored a 2008 paper stating that the majority of deaths in the 1918–1919 influenza pandemic were caused by secondary bacterial pneumonia. However, there is no evidence—neither in that paper nor in any other source—that Fauci attributed these deaths to wearing masks. The claim adds the phrase "from wearing masks," which is not supported by any of the retrieved evidence; in fact, the evidence explicitly states that mask-wearing was not mentioned as a contributing factor. Therefore, the claim is false in its central assertion.

